[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   Step 082 -- same-patch geocentric control.
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   step_081 showed that in-cap comets are observed preferentially toward
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   the anti-axis sky region (geocentric resultant R = 0.73): a sky-
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   localized astrometric systematic is therefore not excluded on geometry
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   alone.  This step closes the loophole with a matched-patch design.
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   Two comets observed from the SAME geocentric sky position near
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   perihelion epoch are exposed to the same zonal catalogue error, the
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   same crowding statistics, and the same reduction geometry -- but a
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   temporal boundary acts on the comet's APHELION direction, which is set
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   by the orbit, not by where Earth stood.  The two hypotheses therefore
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   make different predictions inside one observed patch:
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   sky-systematic : discrepancy tracks the observed direction; comets
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   seen in the affected patch carry the anomaly
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   regardless of aphelion direction.
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   temporal wall  : discrepancy tracks the aphelion direction; inside
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   the patch the in-cap members remain discrepant and
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   the out-of-cap members do not.
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   Per-comet data are joined from two measured products:
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   step_b46_geocentric_null.csv   geocentric unit direction at the
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   perihelion epoch (DE440s), and theta,
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   the aphelion-direction angle to the
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   resident axis (49,-17);
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   step_b27_planet_nine_insertion.csv
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   d_of, the catalogue orig->future
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   periapsis rotation (the anomaly
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   channel used by every Phase-3 step).
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   Solar elongation and the galactic latitude of the observed direction
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   are recomputed per comet from DE440s so the two classic observation-
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   geometry channels enter as continuous covariates.
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   Tests
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   1. matched patch: among comets observed within 60 deg of the anti-axis
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   (the patch where the in-cap cohort is seen), in-cap vs out-of-cap
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   d_of (Mann-Whitney) -- the systematic predicts equality;
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   2. restricted gradient: within the patch, Spearman(theta_aph, d_of) --
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   the systematic predicts a flat gradient;
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   3. partial Spearman: d_of vs axis alignment A = cos(theta_aph)
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   controlling observed-patch alignment G = cos(geo_sep), and the
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   mirror -- which predictor retains the signal;
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   4. elongation and galactic-latitude channels: correlation with d_of
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   and in/out-cap contrasts;
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   5. double-dissociation table: median d_of in the (cap x patch) cells.
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   Outputs
[2026-09-21 14:53:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 082]   results/step_b47_sky_matched.json
